#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128924 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/id #uuid "53185b25-c690-500a-9a82-c18b37668e27" :question/math-academy-id "e-6106" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} xy\\ \\!e^{x+y}\\ \\textrm d A$ over the rectangle $R= [0,1] \\times [1,2].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  xy\\  e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big( x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big( y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= \\left(\\int_0^1x\\  e^{x}  \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left( \\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot  \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &=  \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big)\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= 1\\cdot e^2\\[5pt]\n                                                                         &= e^2\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128925 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/id #uuid "a5567cb9-1c16-56a6-b0e8-759edf693a41" :question/math-academy-id "e-6107" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} \\left(x^2-y^2 +3\\right)  \\textrm d A,$  where $R= [-1,3] \\times [2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each of the three integrals.\n\n- The function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(4-2){\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{27}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-(-1)){\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{4}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{224}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function under the third integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}3\\,\\text{d}A=3\\,\\text{Area}(R)=3\\cdot (2\\cdot 4)=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}A=\\frac{56}{3}-\\frac{224}{3}+24=-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128926 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/id #uuid "0cb8fa8a-5be1-5f53-bfde-5acf325f6332" :question/math-academy-id "e-6108" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A$, where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/d96ec9ab40f8f1cadd6d2492dddcc0090f766b72e9c7fdb659e3b2f7f39fce0d.png)\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R = R_1 \\cup R_2,$ where $R_1= (0,2) \\times (-1,0)$ and $R_2= (0,2) \\times (0,1).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\iint\\limits_{R}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R_1} 2 \\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2}    \\dfrac{1}{xy+x+y+1} \\ \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\iint\\limits_{R_1} \\textrm d A\n+ \\iint\\limits_{R_2}  \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)(y+1)} \\ \\textrm d A\\[5pt]\n&= 2(2-0)(0-(-1)) + \\Bigg( \\int_0^2 \\dfrac{1}{x+1} \\ \\textrm d x \\Bigg) \\Bigg( \\int_0^1 \\dfrac{1}{y+1}\\ \\textrm d y \\Bigg) \\[5pt]\n&= 4 + \\Big[\\ln(x+1)\\Big]_0^2  \\cdot \\Big[\\ln(y+1)\\Big]_0^1\\[5pt] \n&= 4+ \\ln 3\\ln 2.\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128942 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "1c227b12-d40b-53a8-b568-b7bd380acbee" :question/math-academy-id "e-7023" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = 8,\n\\qquad\n\\iint\\limits_{D}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = -5,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{C \\cup D}  3f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(8+(-5)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065ad1df-9aa1-5a78-a9b9-15d291248fb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331637} {:answer/id #uuid "364b9c98-896f-5017-b067-62e3f7940078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331638} {:answer/id #uuid "aa956518-1500-54a5-a801-2dbbdde30ad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331639} {:answer/id #uuid "e0718815-7182-5b86-a45b-79031cc02006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331640} {:answer/id #uuid "84c7837c-712b-5a29-9a96-14ef657f6a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "065ad1df-9aa1-5a78-a9b9-15d291248fb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331637} :answer-field/id #uuid "e843a88b-3377-5f11-879e-da4431c7a178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "872f93f5-8409-5a4d-bae6-2b36bd1649e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129936" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d2759bd-2c0e-5834-b285-351dead159e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331644} {:answer/id #uuid "66ac96ee-a558-5ffe-be22-dc81396e0ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331645} {:answer/id #uuid "4bcb4c2b-21b2-52e2-9089-3189c8c5afff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331646} {:answer/id #uuid "52c8ba8c-ec26-52b5-a4dc-0af2d8fdbaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331647} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cf049d-3cb8-51fb-9878-6dbf640d46ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bcb4c2b-21b2-52e2-9089-3189c8c5afff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331646} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b38fe9-2e4b-514c-bad7-3ffc002f4930" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8258a072-705e-56a8-9475-6ae8261869c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-129937" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{8}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2ce9cf6-cb89-5925-be70-58d120a18f3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331651} {:answer/id #uuid "a9864cbf-6a64-53cc-ab8e-c71fa558a57d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331652} {:answer/id #uuid "3a758cc8-944e-5221-8cb4-2dff9b804d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331653} {:answer/id #uuid "76966019-65c6-5468-9ee2-9d79dbf3bfbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331654} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6f7c7e-5ffb-562c-95fb-be585d8fd4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2ce9cf6-cb89-5925-be70-58d120a18f3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331651} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce1bfa0-20a6-5068-8b84-06cc21216d1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8690565-98c6-57c3-b910-e43d247b53bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130020" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=12,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-8,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(12-8) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07450087-4572-5e4b-befb-2e575d0585d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331658} {:answer/id #uuid "50852e90-d6ac-5628-b55a-1558c854bbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331659} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5b2f99-0f81-5fdf-bd36-1ed010d39ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331660} {:answer/id #uuid "81c6a360-92b9-5f45-8b88-a0bb092cb943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331661} {:answer/id #uuid "308f7e81-3c8e-5242-bff1-f4998dfeb3ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50852e90-d6ac-5628-b55a-1558c854bbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331659} :answer-field/id #uuid "43fca8e7-bd92-521c-a213-0f8e07a7b01f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09109a55-6e5b-5bb8-a3bc-8b73ba148056" :question/math-academy-id "q-130025" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/ddc6c02aff017b31dd24ba6d47a3527aa46a2a5130cffc7094122545babd7656.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ {e}^{x+y}, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5f9e260-1a1d-579f-9b57-a15fbd84f7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(2,4)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331665} {:answer/id #uuid "0b5a9024-0e75-5ff5-ac3a-62b813e9d335" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331666} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d82e3c-5c20-54ab-aa37-e417510f61b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,4)}(\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331667} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2c6498-0bbc-51b1-8d61-66f647a3cbbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}(y+1)}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331668} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd9a671-a4ed-5690-8200-2b1dcd65bbef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b5a9024-0e75-5ff5-ac3a-62b813e9d335" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331666} :answer-field/id #uuid "024c2b39-8277-583c-ac44-4c2691bc49bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa545ca3-9563-54ed-9285-b7780bc32dbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130038" :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<2,\\,1<y<2, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<2,\\,2<y<4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,4)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(1,2)\\times ((1,2)\\cup (2,4)) \\\\  & =((1,2)\\times (1,2))\\cup ((1,2)\\times (2,4)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331670 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff3b9225-4648-526f-9d5f-127e85a0572c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331672} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1d25ff-26e6-5cb0-83fd-b2343ac16372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331673} {:answer/id #uuid "21eaf458-fe5e-5fca-9276-194a8a42b149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331674} {:answer/id #uuid "8a072d07-788a-5b8a-8aad-313ac5a77db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi /2)\\times (0,\\pi /2)}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(\\pi /2,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331675} {:answer/id #uuid "baa3a292-1bc7-55a8-bf22-2f719e14a0d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{(0,\\pi )}\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{(0,\\pi /2)}y{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b1d25ff-26e6-5cb0-83fd-b2343ac16372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331673} :answer-field/id #uuid "03d42796-79f8-5bb3-85ce-6a171bb6bae1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e54cf7f9-2631-5a16-9687-837a1b22c094" :question/math-academy-id "q-130039" :question/problem "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<\\pi ,\\,0<y<\\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ \\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y,\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(0,\\pi )\\times ((0,\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =((0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\cup ((0,\\pi )\\times (\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (0,\\pi /4)}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{(0,\\pi )\\times (\\pi /4,\\pi /2)}\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffba388d-4ee9-5cae-b02c-12e454d9897d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331679} {:answer/id #uuid "2bc7675f-8727-5068-b0a0-d9b7166646e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331680} {:answer/id #uuid "67b3f714-6193-5acd-ac0f-9fac0b9e06e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331681} {:answer/id #uuid "9efc95d2-2ab1-59a1-ba7e-ab01afcc6304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331682} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf2ff69-0e27-56a6-b0a2-7a8d0ab392eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffba388d-4ee9-5cae-b02c-12e454d9897d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331679} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb65359e-1fd4-55e9-8c70-eab9287fafd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e63b0a5-7cfb-5161-99b4-9fc71f17af1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130042" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<2, \\\\ 2x,\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,0<y<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(-2,0)\\times (0,2)$ and ${R}_{2}=(0,1)\\times (0,2).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}(x)({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}2x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{-2}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)+(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2}+2[{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}+2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2775855-e58c-5e5a-ac1d-cc0258739b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-e+14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331686} {:answer/id #uuid "4e274f70-1c1d-5fdb-8184-7f76ec4b5274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331687} {:answer/id #uuid "814601c4-e338-5be0-8685-a4d9bf7a2b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{2}+2e-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331688} {:answer/id #uuid "22f26f18-16e1-5f3b-aa74-cbb48af144e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{2}+2e-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331689} {:answer/id #uuid "e858bec8-ab90-51c7-8c57-fdae0465fc6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{2}-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22f26f18-16e1-5f3b-aa74-cbb48af144e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{2}+2e-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331689} :answer-field/id #uuid "2240a951-f4d8-57c4-94fc-4aca5062f755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98269be4-2afe-5dec-b8d7-d94389e0ed6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130044" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y{e}^{x+1},\\, & \\text{if}\\,0<x<1,\\,-2<y<0, \\\\ 3y\\sqrt{x},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<4,\\,-2<y<0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(0,1)\\times (-2,0)$ and ${R}_{2}=(1,4)\\times (-2,0).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}y{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}3y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}({e}^{x+1})(y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}(\\sqrt{x})(3y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,\\text{d}y)+({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-2}^{0}3y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[{e}^{x+1}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[\\frac{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}]}_{1}^{4}\\cdot {[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =({e}^{2}-e)\\cdot (0-2)+(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3})\\cdot (0-6) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2}+2e-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fece8aa-41df-52a5-8c21-d1ef3d25a395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128487} {:answer/id #uuid "a20ce637-1626-5222-8e33-7802082782b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128488} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4c985e-7cdb-5913-bc8b-2dc1f996dd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128489} {:answer/id #uuid "515a563d-b414-5e28-95bf-e95e519da264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1 - e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128490} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6efdf4-2d6d-5cb5-8f5d-363e91370ee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c6efdf4-2d6d-5cb5-8f5d-363e91370ee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(e - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128491} :answer-field/id #uuid "41147118-a5f5-5fa1-9e40-8dc3957ccf01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8826be0-32c0-5213-809c-c90ea8221b73" :question/math-academy-id "q-71932" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{ }({e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =2(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129810 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6afde6c2-fb30-5fd6-99e3-2bcc107620e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}y\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331692} {:answer/id #uuid "6f52deaa-7e54-50ba-948d-1579588cc718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331693} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3c0eeb-39e0-50b5-b3c5-b1d45576f18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331694} {:answer/id #uuid "e638328c-095b-50a0-ba86-e137d2b8b5a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}(x+{x}^{2}y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331695} {:answer/id #uuid "8a737a23-ee2a-524f-b409-b9d7f3b26cfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f52deaa-7e54-50ba-948d-1579588cc718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331693} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f5d3229-4c0b-5422-b900-ee90e915e973" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e01cd29-3b44-5c08-bc75-551f046b44dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-80452" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/ed0be2aca8d43d733e91f3a8feaaca0649957dcbd516a8218b1e7dea136170d8.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ {x}^{2}y, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1392ce5a-c7dc-51cf-abdd-1eadcc8cfe62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331699} {:answer/id #uuid "475b2988-f992-5987-8d78-d13670fd5b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331700} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbc925f-02c6-531f-8594-4c79f771d206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331701} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe512f6-d890-5944-97a6-11cd84a737cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331702} {:answer/id #uuid "b14b81f0-53c9-5437-ac45-6168dc3c5bf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "475b2988-f992-5987-8d78-d13670fd5b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331700} :answer-field/id #uuid "e28026f0-e80f-5451-bef9-67864ea215ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "203634ad-0919-52d0-95c4-311cd1738590" :question/math-academy-id "q-80507" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec44686a-601b-52b3-81df-e57e6708fb93" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Multiplicative Property"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "586bc4dc-bffb-578a-a5fd-f62740023c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}(1-e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331706} {:answer/id #uuid "637da715-3dc2-52d0-a738-8edaa50f1d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331707} {:answer/id #uuid "1cf1f1e4-6da1-5844-a392-2edabec3094f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331708} {:answer/id #uuid "60935b2d-303c-5ec9-a4e4-90da1985a2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}(1-e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331709} {:answer/id #uuid "0a0c8dbb-5526-54cc-b090-3fb53b880816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "637da715-3dc2-52d0-a738-8edaa50f1d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331707} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f7288f-1ac9-55ab-ba65-07ae0151e236" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e94b1a94-0fa1-5def-adbc-05a87d715560" :question/math-academy-id "q-80511" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{y}}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,\\sqrt{3}]\\times [0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{y}}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}})({e}^{y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c736a60-846e-5be0-b49b-bb4f23bcc855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331713} {:answer/id #uuid "a30499b3-8cb2-5945-b930-2684db62c938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331714} {:answer/id #uuid "3d09b270-867d-5bd4-8ed3-f4416641770e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331715} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e3e8c3-9e9b-53e9-a3db-f6e8fdd3777d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331716} {:answer/id #uuid "7814dc03-11b9-5567-9501-5eca5940d0ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d09b270-867d-5bd4-8ed3-f4416641770e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331715} :answer-field/id #uuid "950f08cb-58ec-532b-b7f6-946277e6b610" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "654ce247-5ae0-50de-879f-ff6be0880366" :question/math-academy-id "q-80626" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[0,3]\\times [0,2].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A=2\\,\\text{Area}(R)=2\\cdot (3\\cdot 2)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A & =(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot [{x}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2({3}^{2}-(0)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the third integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3\\cdot [{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=12+18-24=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4eb38d-2263-5662-b7bc-97900c473302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331720} {:answer/id #uuid "6344c30c-7da7-5f67-88ea-0b7dae0cf25c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331721} {:answer/id #uuid "276ad511-5dad-520e-87e9-57b70df049a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331722} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ebab3e-d54e-51ba-8bd4-27166789830d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331723} {:answer/id #uuid "47fb5657-e78c-5c1f-a25c-4a2c8c35e82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6344c30c-7da7-5f67-88ea-0b7dae0cf25c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331721} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d1d8f99-e8f2-5c7b-8e3c-1a377dc16933" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331719}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "919b89cb-fe14-5b02-9e23-6f5514b0dbda" :question/math-academy-id "q-80627" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{2+6y{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [2,4].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{2+6y{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+6y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}6y\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & =(4-2){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{x}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{2}-(-\\frac{2}{1})) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}6y\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{2}^{4}6y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =3({4}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{2+6y{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A=2+36=38.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5f92e0e-005e-504d-9e39-8198a21f6536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331727} {:answer/id #uuid "9e08b9d9-e52d-5fa2-8bbd-89251a618049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331728} {:answer/id #uuid "13d84dfc-e8c3-574f-a3d0-7506b62fe7c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331729} {:answer/id #uuid "f85f63d1-aec3-5519-9943-d94619c17fc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331730} {:answer/id #uuid "20a17648-745e-50da-90c0-be6a556ab998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20a17648-745e-50da-90c0-be6a556ab998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331731} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4e0cc94-8b1d-5c5a-8912-05664bf0d40a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a911bd-93f1-5923-a96a-66a07b9142e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-80638" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(6{x}^{2}-10{y}^{4})\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[-2,0]\\times [-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(6{x}^{2}-10{y}^{4})\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}6{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}10{y}^{4}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}6{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(1-(-1)){\\int }_{-2}^{0}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2{x}^{3}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot {0}^{3}-2\\cdot (-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}10{y}^{4}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(0-(-2)){\\int }_{-1}^{1}10{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2{y}^{5}{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot {1}^{5}-2\\cdot (-1)^{5}) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(6{x}^{2}+10{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}A=32-8=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "769163af-fbff-5e30-ab5d-313cd4974238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331734} {:answer/id #uuid "27aac87d-6bb1-5074-bcfa-6596ee4d1c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T\\cup U}\\frac{x+y}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331735} {:answer/id #uuid "85f09bde-57f9-5321-90ec-ee3426f98d60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331736} {:answer/id #uuid "1262f3c7-07db-5453-bc0e-3d0dc277c56a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}\\frac{x+y}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331737} {:answer/id #uuid "cf39364c-de01-54e0-99c3-c1f890e0ab82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T\\cup U}\\frac{x+y}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "769163af-fbff-5e30-ab5d-313cd4974238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331734} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e981341-9608-502f-9647-15441753fe50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eea6b611-00bb-5f83-baaa-40b71dbd134d" :question/math-academy-id "q-80660" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/939f859ef3454e31a9adaae7d72210ef670f93cbf3d77ecf87aa3879d8d0644c.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ \\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ \\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd" :knowledge-point/title "Using Additivity of Double Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c82fadb1-6b06-5934-a75c-e331b66e0c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331741} {:answer/id #uuid "d3595b6a-4053-5bc5-97a6-7f2ffde489c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331742} {:answer/id #uuid "a4287213-9eac-55f1-8d77-e28769b1a69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331743} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6f3469-8b02-5bb6-a65a-4f5e928ba94c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331744} {:answer/id #uuid "0e6058b3-deb7-5a21-a099-0317a2feaa64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4287213-9eac-55f1-8d77-e28769b1a69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331743} :answer-field/id #uuid "4031b93d-ce9f-5ee0-b4a2-e72bdb76b97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d34b0049-3b85-5ba9-bbfe-6ab88f4f0f19" :question/math-academy-id "q-80661" :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\\frac{1}{2},\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\\frac{3}{2},\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{f(x,y)}{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{f(x,y)}{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "988ee327-4bf2-5fbf-991c-51f874065693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12-15e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331748} {:answer/id #uuid "4841591a-03d2-5cfa-80af-80fbd0491d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-15e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331749} {:answer/id #uuid "6f52f616-acc9-5cac-9997-a3db51a1ccca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18e-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331750} {:answer/id #uuid "431fd19b-3d4d-5c5f-8063-f63b468621eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-12e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331751} {:answer/id #uuid "1215dade-8beb-59ba-8ed4-df07826cb508" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15e-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4841591a-03d2-5cfa-80af-80fbd0491d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-15e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331749} :answer-field/id #uuid "36835f30-7d82-5080-9230-15da409493fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b17aeae-345a-5d7a-904d-6b5cb3dd86f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-81243" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [1,e].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{3}{y}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(e-1)[{x}^{4}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({2}^{4}-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =15(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A=3-15(e-1)=18-15e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "307bccb6-036f-51bb-99ce-327aad8dfdbe" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral When the Integrand Contains Only One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ae4fc5c-5552-5293-b8b8-3c55edfc9901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331755} {:answer/id #uuid "cad00951-8f7c-5dd9-b258-0fab9f58bdf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "306" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331756} {:answer/id #uuid "14a2892c-6482-5b62-86b8-207c7e6cbebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "271" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331757} {:answer/id #uuid "b50c858a-5663-5e08-b302-9e82185219a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331758} {:answer/id #uuid "31ad1d6d-04a7-5a1b-bde3-6563c3a22eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "243" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ae4fc5c-5552-5293-b8b8-3c55edfc9901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331755} :answer-field/id #uuid "86a21dc0-883a-5e25-ac9f-03459c28f5b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1adca866-e43f-5fb1-b3ea-e60c847c71ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-81245" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[2,5]\\times [0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}4{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}2x\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(5-2){\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3[{y}^{4}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3({3}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =243.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{2}^{5}2x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3[{x}^{2}]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =3({5}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}A=243-63=180.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8059a197-e9fb-5306-8eed-62c0cea88f33" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Double Integral Using the Additivity Over a Rectangular Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6554e9b4-6442-59c0-a7a3-7f1104e5b7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331762} {:answer/id #uuid "58a9aba8-0a49-5b12-9458-6bdc156cb98b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331763} {:answer/id #uuid "3287fca3-a939-5044-974b-70186b602e8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331764} {:answer/id #uuid "92e9d5e8-4b49-52ae-ad13-cd20337cafee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331765} {:answer/id #uuid "b3585656-2fff-5a3e-b7f6-0d010dbba793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3585656-2fff-5a3e-b7f6-0d010dbba793" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331766} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4e0561f-a25d-5086-9993-48e800e4d203" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e2470ce-d831-5f07-9d5c-ccac4591a05a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81254" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<9,\\,-1<y<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{xy}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<9,\\,1<y<4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2}$, where ${R}_{1}=(1,9)\\times (-1,1)$ and ${R}_{2}=(1,9)\\times (1,4).$ So, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A= & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{R}_{1}}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{R}_{2}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =(9-1){\\int }_{-1}^{1}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+({\\int }_{1}^{9}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =8[{y}^{3}]_{-1}^{1}+[\\sqrt{x}]_{1}^{9}\\cdot [\\sqrt{y}]_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =8({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3})+(3-1)\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
